{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/937503-wonder-101","id":937503,"title":"Wonder 101","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-26T00:18:28-07:00","id":937503,"title":"Wonder 101","content":"Hi, I've been reading lately about Wonders in &quot;Forged by Dragon's Fire&quot; and in M20, but I took notice that there might be several differences, so I couldn't quite grasp it completely how a Wonder is made.<br /> <br /> Seeing this as example:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022 Trushades (Trinket)<br /> <br /> Arete N/A, Quintessence N/A, Background Cost 2-6 pts.<br /> <br /> In a simple, yet potentially powerful, variation on the old<br /> \u201cX-ray specs\u201d concept, many mages keep glasses or goggles that<br /> have been modified with between one and three perceptual<br /> Effects. The name Trushades comes from a variety marketed to<br /> Awakened customers by Greer Laboratories \u2013 a cabal composed<br /> of Ecstatic, Etherite, and VA mages whose slogan is \u201cLook<br /> closer.\u201d Other, generic varieties exist under many different<br /> names. Although such shades \u2013 which range from simple reading<br /> glasses or sunglasses to stylish shades and wild eyewear \u2013 look<br /> perfectly normal, their enhancements allow the wearer to view<br /> things no human eyes should be able to see.<br /> <br /> System: Depending upon the Spheres involved, a pair of<br /> Trushades can employ any Rank 1 visual perception Effect. The<br /> most common variations incorporate Forces (electrons or other<br /> physical energies), Life (overall health and the presence of life),<br /> Matter (the structure of inanimate items and surfaces), Mind<br /> (auras), and Prime (Quintessence and Resonance/ Synergy<br /> forces), but really \u2013 any visually perceivable Sphere works.<br /> <br /> Generally, a pair of modified glasses also features an<br /> activation word or touch; this way, the wearer can turn the<br /> Effects on and off at will. A one-dot pair holds a single Effect,<br /> and the three-dot sets feature three different Spheres working<br /> toward a single purpose. Three Spheres, however, is the<br /> maximum capacity for a non-Talisman pair of glasses\u2026 and any<br /> character who tries to use all three Spheres at once will suffer<br /> both a -2 penalty to her Perception rolls and a nasty (though<br /> non-injurious) headache. </div> </div> </div>So, as far as I understood, you can make a Trinket with one-two-three Effects and keep it at that, without having to spend Quintessence or roll Wonder's Arete (which is not so good to be honest. Wonders usually have unimpressive Arete and you're forced to difficulty of 6).<br /> <br /> Me and few other Mage players were discussing possibillity of other custom Wonders, and here's what we came up with:<br /> <br /> Our characters are Verbena, Dreamspeaker and Euthanatos. We follow &quot;Creation is Innately Alive and Divine&quot; belief (which is quite common for our Traditions), so we planned to create a tattoo-trinket with picture of panther on character's back that blesses with speed of a wild cat. (Game-wise speaking, we read chapter that certain Sphere Effects can simulate Gifts. There's a rote of Correspondence 1 + Time 1 Effect to increase your initiative, and we wanted to copy the Effect from Gift &quot;Spirit of the Fray&quot;. Basically, that tattoo as trinket will passively give +10 to initiative, just like this rank 2 Gift does.)<br /> <br /> I don't see any reason why this cannot be legit (considering that the example with Trushades above directly from M20 book says that Trinkets always carry the Effect of spells passively), but I'd like to ask anyway if this idea is decent or it just won't do. We decided that tattoo as Trinket could do because it fits our practice &quot;Bodywork&quot; and &quot;Artwork&quot;.<br /> <br /> What do you think about this and why? Is there any additional info about crafting Wonders, and if yes, where? (except &quot;Forged by Dragon's Fire)<br /> <br /> Oh and as bonus, if you've got any ideas for Wonders, we'd greatly appreciate it! We have plenty on our own, but we sometimes doubt if they're legitimate.<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12132-bogdan","name":"Bogdan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T02:06:27-07:00","id":937516,"title":"","content":"The Trushades are broken, in the way that they are not actually a Trinket by the definition of Trinkets.<br /> Trinkets are supposed to be normal items, with a magickal effect having changed their properties. They themselves are not technically magickal at all,<br /> The Trushades however get 'activated' with a word or touch. This makes them a triggered Wonder(!), not a trinket. Trinkets have no effect on them. They simply got permanently changed somehow.<br /> <br /> But, aside of that:<br /> <br /> Tattoos-as-a-trinket does not make sense.<br /> <br /> Here's why:<br /> As stated above, trinkets are normal objects that got changed or enhanced with an effect. They themselves are not inherently magickal. Basically you have normal objects, whose normal properties got changed.<br /> <br /> A hoodie that's bulletproof. Glasses that constantly give you night vision by showing infrared falling through them.<br /> How are the changed properties of the tattoos supposed to give extra speed?<br /> <br /> So, tattoos can't really be a trinket that gives you extra speed, no. You can make tattoos a trinket by making them change colors. Or making the tattoos be a substance that hardens on impact, forming a sort of exotic armor (which sounds kind of horribly painful...might be a bad idea)<br /> <br /> For extra speed, just skip the tattoo phase and cast an effect with a long duration on the person themselves <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Or what you want to do is, turn the tattoos into a full wonder. That would work perfectly for your purposes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 07-26-2016, 05:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T02:44:11-07:00","id":937524,"title":"","content":"Oh I see.<br /> <br /> The sole reason why it's tattoo is because I assumed it could fit under paradigm. Thanks for clearing it up.<br /> <br /> Would it work for the purpose of Wonder then? As in, an activation of some sort (like you pointed out with Trushades) that would trigger the Effect? And I suppose using it would drain 1 Quintessence per usage from the Wonder, thus this tattoo has to be &quot;refueled&quot; from time to time? Or, could it be kept active passively (much like Trushades I think?), and kept.. well, active.<br /> <br /> While we're at the usage of Quintessence for such Effects, there's example of minor tattoo-Wonder in &quot;Forged by Dragon's Fire&quot; where Mage has his arms (possibly with legs too) covered in some sort of claw-looking tattoos. What it does is turn user's Brawl/ Martial Arts damage into aggravated through application of Prime 2 as soon as it's activated (and user has to spend 1 Quintessence from Wonder which drains it, if I got the description right), but he does not roll anything.<br /> <br /> I wondered what would be the &quot;stretch&quot; of such Wonders. Could one create some similar tattoo (or well, any Wonder, just as long as it fits Mage's paradigm according to M20's guide to using Wonders) that contains Time 3 Effect within, providing user with +2 additional actions everytime a Quintessence point is spent from the Wonder? It sounds like quite a strong Wonder, but not <i>that</i> strong at same time (heh), considering that simple cocaine/ meth/ speed drugs already provide anybody with +1 additional action per turn for hours (as long as drug's effect lasts).<br /> <br /> What do you think about that?<br /> <br /> P.S: Well true lmao, we could just do long Duration Effect probably, but I'm just trying to grasp concept on how Wonders work so I'd not fall into doing mistake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12132-bogdan","name":"Bogdan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T03:00:23-07:00","id":937527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bogdan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/937503-wonder-101?p=937524#post937524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh I see.<br /> <br /> The sole reason why it's tattoo is because I assumed it could fit under paradigm. Thanks for clearing it up.<br /> <br /> Would it work for the purpose of Wonder then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup yup. The old Mage Revised ed books even had examples of Mages turning their tattoos into wonders. It can be VERY befitting some paradigms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> More stuff </div> </div> </div>Careful <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Dragon's Fire and M20 Wonder rules are not inherently compatible.<br /> <br /> With the M20-described Wonder (As in, Talismans/Devices) process, Wonders don't necessarily spend Quintessence, but basically their Arete roll determines the duration, potency etc. of the unleashed effect. (I highly prefer this)<br /> <br /> With Dragon's Fire, a single success on the Arete roll unleashes the 'Full Effect', but sadly Dragon's Fire is broken in the way that it never describes how things like duration et al are handled. Yay.<br /> <br /> And both systems suck at explaining just when or how it's determined if using a Wonder requires expenditure of Quintessence or not.<br /> <br /> I really hope the M20 Book Of Secrets will clear things up more regarding M20 Wonder creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 07-26-2016, 06:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T03:09:12-07:00","id":937530,"title":"","content":"Hm, I'd assume Wonder's activation also takes an action? That doesn't make them very impressive, considering they're forced to stay at difficulty of 6. (Whereas a smart or skilled willworker could drop that difficulty to make more potent Effect without help of any Wonder)<br /> <br /> If one were to roll Wonder's Effect at Arete 5 let's say (and we can assume it has that Time 3 Effect), does it take an action or turn to get it running? Could one use it through application &quot;Violence as Focus&quot; (with fitting Focus obviously) or reflexively to have a normal action + Arete roll (coming from one-self) in that case?<br /> <br /> I did hear somewhere that Wonders do not take an action to be activated (though I'm not sure at all about this and decided to ask here before I do anything with them at all), is that true? If they do take an action, then.. well yeah, they're not that impressive it seems then due to reason stated above (or I might be missing out something).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12132-bogdan","name":"Bogdan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T03:17:54-07:00","id":937532,"title":"","content":"To add:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bogdan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/937503-wonder-101?p=937524#post937524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What it does is turn user's Brawl/ Martial Arts damage into aggravated through application of Prime 2 as soon as it's activated (and user has to spend 1 Quintessence from Wonder which drains it, if I got the description right), but he does not roll anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, that's something that isn't properly explained. A Wonder that does not get rolled. Careful with Wonder examples. Stick to the rules instad of the examples.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T03:41:04-07:00","id":937538,"title":"","content":"Thanks for clearing out. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Though, regarding the question above:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If one were to roll Wonder's Effect at Arete 5 let's say (and we can assume it has that Time 3 Effect), does it take an action or turn to get it running? Could one use it through application &quot;Violence as Focus&quot; (with fitting Focus obviously) or reflexively to have a normal action + Arete roll (coming from one-self) in that case? </div> </div> </div>General information I found about using Wonders:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Using a Wonder<br /> <br /> As a general rule, Devices and Talismans have their own<br /> Enlightenment/ Arete Trait, which determines the dice pool for<br /> the item\u2019s Effects. If Ryan uses a 4 Arete bafflejack, for example,<br /> his player rolls four dice to activate that Talisman\u2019s Effect. </div> </div> </div>Due to fact it says &quot;Devices and Talismans have their own Enlightenment/ Arete trait&quot;, does it imply you can use Wonder <i>and</i> make your own Arete roll within a single turn, or using a Wonder takes an action?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12132-bogdan","name":"Bogdan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T04:23:42-07:00","id":937546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bogdan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/937503-wonder-101?p=937538#post937538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Due to fact it says &quot;Devices and Talismans have their own Enlightenment/ Arete trait&quot;, does it imply you can use Wonder <i>and</i> make your own Arete roll within a single turn, or using a Wonder takes an action?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep yep yep.<br /> Wonders and hanging effects made with Time 4 are the two ways that a Mage can fire off multiple effects in a single round.<br /> <br /> Of course it depends, fluff-wise, on the nature of the wonder.<br /> A staff that you need to shake around while shouting &quot;Cthulhu is my homeboy!&quot; will hardly leave you the time to also employ a focus for another effect in the same round, but wonders that basically are simply mentally triggered or react to circumstances are reflexive to use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T04:40:31-07:00","id":937548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A staff that you need to shake around while shouting &quot;Cthulhu is my homeboy!&quot; </div> </div> </div>sides = gone<br /> <br /> You made my day. Thanks for clearing out so much and answering a lot lately, greatly appreciated. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12132-bogdan","name":"Bogdan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T04:58:34-07:00","id":937551,"title":"","content":"My pleasure! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T13:37:44-07:00","id":937746,"title":"","content":"Alternatively, an 'always on' artifact could do your speed boost tattoos handily. But it's much harder to make those than a standard trinket.<br /> <br /> And what do you mean wonders have less than impressive Arete scores?<br /> <br /> Artifacts use your own personal Arete. And only require one success to succeed. Or alternatively, you can build them a bit more and have them simply be 'always active' The standard +1 sword.<br /> <br /> Charms require you roll Arete beforehand, and again, only require one success to accomplish the effect, though they are single use.<br /> <br /> Talismans use their own Arete yes, but the Arete Score on them is limited only to how much Tass you funnel into them. There's no reason you can't make a Talisman with an Arete score of 100 save for practicality. It's not hard to get more reasonable but still potent arete scores in them. AND they also only need one success.<br /> <br /> Wonders are by and far the easiest way to cast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T21:09:22-07:00","id":937920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/937503-wonder-101?p=937746#post937746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no reason you can't make a Talisman with an Arete score of 100 save for practicality. It's not hard to get more reasonable but still potent arete scores in them. AND they also only need one success.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on wether you use M20 or Dragon's Fire rules;<br /> <br /> In M20, Arete score equals Background Dots of the Wonder, and Background Dots equal the highest sphere used for the Talisman effect.<br /> Optionally a higher Arete score can be infused by using a higher Background rating for the Wonder, despite the lower effect, with all requirements adjusted for the higher rating.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, you bring up my main problem with Dragon's Fire:<br /> You only need 'one success' to fully trigger a Talisman's effect in Dragon's Fire. But if you roll that one success, what's the actual efficiency and score of the Wonder's effect? Duration? Damage? Targets etc. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> There is no roll for the Effect at creation time.<br /> <br /> P.s.<br /> And just as a logical houserule, I would say that a Wonder's Arete cannot be higher than the Arete of the Mage that created it. It just makes sense, theme-wise. You cannot put more metaphysical excellence into an item than you, yourself, even comprehend and possess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 07-27-2016, 01:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T22:42:52-07:00","id":937945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/937503-wonder-101?p=937920#post937920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And just as a logical houserule, I would say that a Wonder's Arete cannot be higher than the Arete of the Mage that created it. It just makes sense, theme-wise. You cannot put more metaphysical excellence into an item than you, yourself, even comprehend and possess.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems reasonable on the face of it, but it also means that all those Enlightenment 8 plasma cannons have the personal, dedicated attention of an E8 Enlightened Scientist in the Inner Circle/Control handcrafting every one in order to get... three more damage dice.<br /> <br /> Same with Deep Space Combat Armor and its Enlightenment 6 rating.<br /> <br /> This is someone who, using the Revised system, is <i>so posthumanly enlightened</i> that they can potentially totally disregard things like needing to use technology and the boundaries between Sphere training. Making plasma cannons slightly more efficient.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T23:45:11-07:00","id":937959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quantumboost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/937503-wonder-101?p=937945#post937945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That seems reasonable on the face of it, but it also means that all those Enlightenment 8 plasma cannons have the personal, dedicated attention of an E8 Enlightened Scientist in the Inner Circle/Control handcrafting every one in order to get... three more damage dice</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind you that under M20 rules, forces adds a *level* of damage (not a point), and that every Arete success means 2 damage.<br /> An Arete 8 plasma cannon in M20 would equal possibly 18 aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> ...yeeah.<br /> <br /> That said, I can also see *<i>multiple</i>* Mages working on a single wonder (And really, especially in the Technocratic paradigms, why *shouldn't* they?), and thus the max achievable Arete rating of the wonder equalling the combined Arete of those that work on it. The Technocracy doesn't have a single scientist work on a cannon from start to finish. And everybody can bring in some excellence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T23:58:09-07:00","id":937964,"title":"","content":"And it stands to reason that even an Enlightenment 10 cannon is not really as enlightened as an arete 1 mage.<br /> <br /> The score is more of a power value.<br /> It is no problem giving higher scores than you personally can access, your wonder can only do what you can do, but often faster.<br /> This gives a(nother) reason to make wonders for personal use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T00:03:34-07:00","id":937967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/937503-wonder-101?p=937964#post937964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is no problem giving higher scores than you personally can access, your wonder can only do what you can do, but often faster.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well. In a way..yeah, that's actually quite right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T00:09:28-07:00","id":937969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/937503-wonder-101?p=937959#post937959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind you that under M20 rules, forces adds a *level* of damage (not a point), and that every Arete success means 2 damage.<br /> An Arete 8 plasma cannon in M20 would equal possibly 18 aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> ...yeeah.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. The substantive thing there was more &quot;what the extra Enlightenment gives you is just more fire, not actually any sort of transcendent capability or flexibility like a <i>real</i> Enlightenment score gives a person&quot;.<br /> <br /> &quot;Pooling&quot; Enlightenment between creators in much the way that ritual-casting does seems entirely reasonable as an explanation. And also means that ItX's and the Progenitors' (for examples) &quot;we can just get a bunch of us together, say what we're doing, and then do it&quot; paradigmatic solidarity is probably extra terrifying in terms of Wonder-making...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T05:01:53-07:00","id":938031,"title":"","content":"Hey guys. Sorry to butt in this thread but I ended up getting curious if wonders allow for extended casting; let's say I have a Wonder by M20's rules which possesses a conjunctional effect of Correspondence 1 + Time 1 (Arete rating for the Wonder is 2), which gives someone one extra point in their initiative per success. Would such a Wonder allow for casting successfully (several rolls), until you built up a decent effect; for example, getting 5 successes, dedicating 3 to +3 inititive, and 2 for its Duration to last a scene?<br /> <br /> Also, what is the difficulty of the roll for the Wonder? Do you roll it as an Coincidental effect, thus difficulty 1 (from Sphere rank 1) + 3?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12152-rotwood","name":"Rotwood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T09:43:11-07:00","id":938175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rotwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/937503-wonder-101?p=938031#post938031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey guys. Sorry to butt in this thread but I ended up getting curious if wonders allow for extended casting;</div> </div> </div> </div>Undefined, and purely up to houseruling.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, what is the difficulty of the roll for the Wonder? Do you roll it as an Coincidental effect, thus difficulty 1 (from Sphere rank 1) + 3? </div> </div> </div>The normal rules apply, really.<br /> If the effect is coincidental in the circumstances, yes. If not, no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T12:39:05-07:00","id":938276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/937503-wonder-101?p=937920#post937920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Depends on wether you use M20 or Dragon's Fire rules;<br /> <br /> In M20, Arete score equals Background Dots of the Wonder, and Background Dots equal the highest sphere used for the Talisman effect.<br /> Optionally a higher Arete score can be infused by using a higher Background rating for the Wonder, despite the lower effect, with all requirements adjusted for the higher rating.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, you bring up my main problem with Dragon's Fire:<br /> You only need 'one success' to fully trigger a Talisman's effect in Dragon's Fire. But if you roll that one success, what's the actual efficiency and score of the Wonder's effect? Duration? Damage? Targets etc. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> There is no roll for the Effect at creation time.<br /> <br /> P.s.<br /> And just as a logical houserule, I would say that a Wonder's Arete cannot be higher than the Arete of the Mage that created it. It just makes sense, theme-wise. You cannot put more metaphysical excellence into an item than you, yourself, even comprehend and possess.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, not much interested in M20 for a variety of reasons.<br /> <br /> Those are all determined by the effect. Suppose you want a laser gun. It fires a beam of forces damage. Much like anything else, you hash out what's reasonable with your ST and then go. The Go-to Guide I go with is You accomplish the effect. And distribute a number of successes worth of stuff equal Arete + Willpower For Talismans, just their Arete + 1. for things like Damage and Duration and Targets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T00:46:19-07:00","id":939394,"title":"","content":"A quick question, can Wonders receive any sort of difficulty modifiers just like mage? If yes, which ones?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12132-bogdan","name":"Bogdan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T12:28:52-07:00","id":940189,"title":"","content":"I've got a question, in regards of Device Wonders, created my Technomancers. I wonder, as a follower of &quot;Everything is Data&quot; Paradigm, how can one work his way around creating a Wonder? Examples for that, Trushades. My character is a Virtual Adept who follows that paradigm. Here's my question: While creating the device, lets say, goggles to go along the example of Trushades, while giving properties, does he play with the programming of the electrical curcits by giving them new properties, aka, creating a program that might help override the mundane usage of such Device or merely play with the mechanics of the device during creation, believing that it would help him see the &quot;Data&quot; in things and thus giving them such effects? I'm confused on which option to pick while creating the Device Wonder following the Virtual Adept paradigm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12188-theexplosivearrow","name":"TheExplosiveArrow","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T03:12:01-07:00","id":940553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheExplosiveArrow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/937503-wonder-101?p=940189#post940189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've got a question, in regards of Device Wonders, created my Technomancers. I wonder, as a follower of &quot;Everything is Data&quot; Paradigm, how can one work his way around creating a Wonder? Examples for that, Trushades. My character is a Virtual Adept who follows that paradigm. Here's my question: While creating the device, lets say, goggles to go along the example of Trushades, while giving properties, does he play with the programming of the electrical curcits by giving them new properties, aka, creating a program that might help override the mundane usage of such Device or merely play with the mechanics of the device during creation, believing that it would help him see the &quot;Data&quot; in things and thus giving them such effects? I'm confused on which option to pick while creating the Device Wonder following the Virtual Adept paradigm.</div> </div> </div> </div>How you create item itself is up to your belief completely.<br /> <br /> Game-wise, you only enchant the item to hold these certain Effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12132-bogdan","name":"Bogdan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T13:41:21-07:00","id":941379,"title":"","content":"I'd advise reading the book &quot;Off to Be the Wizard&quot; for a decent take on how Virtual Adept hacker magic works. Thematically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T16:10:22-07:00","id":941473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/937503-wonder-101?p=941379#post941379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd advise reading the book &quot;Off to Be the Wizard&quot; for a decent take on how Virtual Adept hacker magic works. Thematically.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looks like a good read, I'll make sure to take a look at it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12188-theexplosivearrow","name":"TheExplosiveArrow","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T20:55:30-07:00","id":962050,"title":"","content":"Do trinkets need Prime to be created, or just any Sphere? In M20 it seems any Sphere can create trinkets, how does this works?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T23:28:06-07:00","id":962126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/937503-wonder-101?p=962050#post962050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do trinkets need Prime to be created, or just any Sphere? In M20 it seems any Sphere can create trinkets, how does this works?</div> </div> </div> </div>Trinkets in M20 are simply items that have been enhanced with an effect. They are not magickal in themselves, and don't really have special rules to create. You're handling everything with normal sphere magick rules.<br /> Put semi-permanent or permanently running effect on object to make it more special/useful = Trinket.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T10:19:43-07:00","id":962353,"title":"","content":"I see. But does it need to be constant or can have an activation? Like make a rock like a grenade with Forces, or a ring that projects a Prime sword.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T10:47:10-07:00","id":962367,"title":"","content":"Anything activation- or event- related in a trinket requires Time 4. It's the reason why the Trushades trinket example in the book isn't actually a trinket. Heh.<br /> <br /> When you make a Trinket, simply do not think of making a trinket; Treat as casting an effect of an object in completely normal ways - It's all you do when making trinkets.They are not real wonders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T11:25:08-07:00","id":962396,"title":"","content":"Got it. But why aren't the trushades trinkets? Where is it said that they can't have an activation?<br /> <br /> I'm remembering an old discussion regarding activation and potions as instruments that i can't remember how it ended. Wouldn't they be similar to making a strength buff potion that is activated when drunk?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T11:38:50-07:00","id":962401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/937503-wonder-101?p=962396#post962396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm remembering an old discussion regarding activation and potions as instruments that i can't remember how it ended. Wouldn't they be similar to making a strength buff potion that is activated when drunk?</div> </div> </div> </div>Potions would be Charms, which are one-use wonders. Sadly the M20 version will get coverage in the Book Of Secrets, not the M20 corebook that we already have.<br /> They're also one-use Charm wonders because they have an activation like that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T11:41:40-07:00","id":962403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/937503-wonder-101?p=962396#post962396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Got it. But why aren't the trushades trinkets? Where is it said that they can't have an activation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Spells' parameters are set at the time of casting the Effect. That's inherent in how they work. It's not 'said' anywhere specifically for Trinkets because 'Trinket' is just a label applied to an object altered by a permanent Effect.<br /> <br /> You might be able to make a spell vary based on its situation with the right sensory Spheres, as a constant-monitoring thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm remembering an old discussion regarding activation and potions as instruments that i can't remember how it ended. Wouldn't they be similar to making a strength buff potion that is activated when drunk? </div> </div> </div>Yes, but to make the potion an actual Trinket rather than casting the spell at the time of drinking, you need Time 4. You cast the Effect when the instrument is used.<br /> <br /> A potion is a <i>complicated</i> instrument that requires prepwork to make, but that's no different from building a machine that you use as an instrument to cast Forces effects.<br /> <br /> Or you can merge the instrument and the Effect completely into a Charm, Artifact, or Talisman, but those are proper Wonders that actually cast spells in their own right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6072,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","user":"Quantumboost","date":". 09-02-2016, 02:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T12:04:57-07:00","id":962422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quantumboost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/937503-wonder-101?p=962403#post962403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spells' parameters are set at the time of casting the Effect. That's inherent in how they work. It's not 'said' anywhere specifically for Trinkets because 'Trinket' is just a label applied to an object altered by a permanent Effect.<br /> You might be able to make a spell vary based on its situation with the right sensory Spheres, as a constant-monitoring thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an intetsting idea. Could the mage enchant the &quot;grenade&quot; with Forces to explode when he shouts a password?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quantumboost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/937503-wonder-101?p=962403#post962403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but to make the potion an actual Trinket rather than casting the spell at the time of drinking, you need Time 4. You cast the Effect when the instrument is used.<br /> <br /> A potion is a <i>complicated</i> instrument that requires prepwork to make, but that's no different from building a machine that you use as an instrument to cast Forces effects.<br /> <br /> Or you can merge the instrument and the Effect completely into a Charm, Artifact, or Talisman, but those are proper Wonders that actually cast spells in their own right.</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference is that the Force effect machine requires a Mage to use it. Are you telling me that if a Mage makes a invisibility potion and hand it to a sleeper, when the sleeper drink it nothing happens? Because a sleeper can't roll Arete.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T12:22:04-07:00","id":962437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/937503-wonder-101?p=962422#post962422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's an intetsting idea. Could the mage enchant the &quot;grenade&quot; with Forces to explode when he shouts a password?</div> </div> </div> </div>Time 4 + Forces. (Forces since it's an audio trigger, and used for the grenade in the first place already. weee.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The difference is that the Force effect machine requires a Mage to use it. Are you telling me that if a Mage makes a invisibility potion and hand it to a sleeper, when the sleeper drink it nothing happens? Because a sleeper can't roll Arete. </div> </div> </div>Exactly. If it's a type of wonder that does not have its own Arete rating, nothing happens.<br /> EXCEPT<br /> If a sleeper is using a wonder that depends on the Mage rolling the Arete, and the Mage is present as the sleeper uses it, I believe that there *is* a chance that the Mage subconciously triggers the wonder - simply depending on their form of paradigm, and because they *believe* it does what it does, and works how it works. It's why witches can happily apply charm potions etc.<br /> <br /> It's also, in a way, an advantage of Time 4 trinkets. They can always trigger for anyone, based on the trigger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T12:38:25-07:00","id":962444,"title":"","content":"Charms/Gadgets can trigger for sleepers. It just costs a willpower point and requires the sleeper believe in the paradigm sufficiently that their witness of the charms events wouldn't cause paradox backlash against themselves.<br /> <br /> Now whether you spend that point every time you use a charm, or if it 'unlocks' a certain variety of charms is ambiguous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T12:43:28-07:00","id":962445,"title":"","content":"- I see. But a cloak of invisibility would be just Forces, right?<br /> <br /> -But the potion isn't a &quot;wonder&quot;, its a trinket/instrument that certainly doesn't have Arete.<br /> I don't buy potionsbonly working with the Mage present using magic subconsciously.<br /> <br /> I'd say that potions don't work for sleepers then...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T12:46:27-07:00","id":962448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/937503-wonder-101?p=962422#post962422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The difference is that the Force effect machine requires a Mage to use it. Are you telling me that if a Mage makes a invisibility potion and hand it to a sleeper, when the sleeper drink it nothing happens? Because a sleeper can't roll Arete.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bingo. Unless it's made in such a way that it can be used by just anyone (which requires any of the already-mentioned methods for doing so, which we've already told you about), <i>something</i> about the potion will make it unusable by Joe Random Sleeper without the Mage's guidance.<br /> <br /> This will always be cast through the lens of the character's paradigm. So maybe the chi-strengthening potion must be tuned to a particular user and consumed in just the right fashion to harmonize with their vital flows.. Maybe it requires you to have an alchemist's altered constitution or it'll just give you mercury poisoning. Maybe it's a harrowing, painful, rapacious mixture and your Will is the only thing that lets you work through the putrefaction phase and come out nobler for the experience. It's on some level up to the player to define how that works in relation to their paradigm.<br /> <br /> If your character's paradigm says that the potions are such that they must necessarily work on everyone, that doesn't automatically let you bypass the Sphere requirements - in fact, it does the opposite. It's a statement that they <i>cannot</i> create potions as instruments in themselves, that they <i>have</i> to make them as Time-delayed Trinkets or Wonders.<br /> <br /> That's not a limitation on potions, it's a limitation on the character and what sort of things they can create within their personal belief structure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T02:02:56-07:00","id":983829,"title":"","content":"Hello, I hope everyone's having a great day.<br /> I was wondering, do you have to have arete 5 to make an arete 5 wonder? in the book it says:-<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As an optional rule, a Wonder may have a higher Arete than<br /> usual; for one extra Background point, that four-dot Talisman<br /> could have an Arete of 5. Generally, Wonders have a capacity<br /> of five Quintessence points for each point of Arete. That fourdot<br /> Arete 5 Talisman, then, could hold up to 25 Quintessence<br /> and would cost nine freebie or experience points. </div> </div> </div>Can it actually exceed the 5 arete rating?<br /> And if so, do you have to roll the spells of each sphere into the wonder while creating it with prime 4 for example having a wonder that can be activated and releases a flames attack or something with forces 3, prime 2 with like 6 successes is that possible or you have to roll the wonder's arete at diff 6 and divide the successes for damage, targets and duration without any reductions or extended rolls with it? (Idk I'm not so experienced with it but if that's the case then that makes wonders so weak)<br /> Or you only roll arete at diff 6 to activate it and release the effect that was created into it like a 6 successes flames bolt released from it once activated and such, idk I need somehelp regarding this matter, and do you need some sphere to make the wonder activate with word or touch? Thanks in advance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12133,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12133-leonardo","user":"Leonardo","date":". 10-08-2016, 05:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12133-leonardo","name":"Leonardo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T21:35:43-07:00","id":984235,"title":"","content":"There's nothing strictly preventing it at least in Forged by Dragon's Fire, and it makes a few Wonders (Technocratic plasma cannons especially) a lot easier to explain if you can build things with higher Arete requirements than you personally have. I'd be unsurprised if STs tended to just assume it was capped at your Arete, though.<br /> <br /> It probably depends on the details of the rotes the wonder includes for how the rolling goes. Firebolts in particular use Forces, so things like area-targeting should be built into what rank of Forces you use for the wonder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6072,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","user":"Quantumboost","date":". 10-09-2016, 12:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T02:17:11-07:00","id":984320,"title":"","content":"So basically it depends on the activation roll of the wonder so like if I got 2 successes for the bolt during activation it will only cause 4 agg + 1 autosuccess for forces, it doesn't matter what rolls I did during the creation for the wonder except for the number of quint spent? Meaning if I rolled 5 successes for the forces rote during the CREATION of the wonder itself it won't launch a 5 successes effect every time I activate it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12133-leonardo","name":"Leonardo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T09:07:33-07:00","id":985455,"title":"","content":"Wonders as written are not so good.<br /> But 6 levels of agg in your example are nothing to sneeze at. Targeting successes come on top.<br /> <br /> If you want to store up big attack spells then Time 4 is your friend. Cast a big nasty spell and freeze it until you trigger it.<br /> Depending on ST charms are also working likewise.<br /> Charms are the only wonders I have seen statted which did a fixed amount of damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}